WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.580
Tokenizer compatibility matters because the model was trained to interpret text through a specific tokenization process.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.689
Special tokens may mark the beginning of text, user messages, assistant messages,

00:00:09.689 --> 00:00:11.402
system prompts, or stop conditions.

00:00:11.402 --> 00:00:15.854
If those tokens are missing or misused, the model may still generate text,

00:00:15.854 --> 00:00:19.964
but it may not follow instructions in the way the user expects.

00:00:19.964 --> 00:00:23.731
Chat templates define how conversational prompts are formatted for a model.

00:00:23.731 --> 00:00:25.786
Two models may both support chat,

00:00:25.786 --> 00:00:29.896
but one may expect a system message in a particular structure while

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:32.293
another expects different role markers or separators.

00:00:32.293 --> 00:00:35.718
A web UI or runtime may apply the template automatically,

00:00:35.718 --> 00:00:38.115
but users should still understand the concept.

00:00:38.115 --> 00:00:41.882
Prompt formatting is part of model compatibility, not just interface style.

00:00:41.882 --> 00:00:45.650
Incorrect formatting can produce weak, oddly structured, or less aligned output.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:50.444
The model may ignore a system instruction, continue a user message instead of answering,

00:00:50.444 --> 00:00:53.184
include unnecessary role labels, or stop too early.

00:00:53.184 --> 00:00:57.979
These issues can look like model quality problems when the real cause is configuration.

00:00:57.979 --> 00:01:02.431
Before blaming a model, verify that the runtime is using the right tokenizer,

00:01:02.431 --> 00:01:04.829
chat template, stop tokens, and context settings.

00:01:04.829 --> 00:01:08.938
Metadata helps runtimes load and use models correctly by carrying facts that

00:01:08.938 --> 00:01:11.336
would otherwise need to be supplied manually.

00:01:11.336 --> 00:01:14.076
It can identify architecture, tokenizer configuration, quantization information,

00:01:14.076 --> 00:01:15.445
and sometimes prompt-related settings.

00:01:15.445 --> 00:01:18.185
Metadata does not remove the need for testing,

00:01:18.185 --> 00:01:22.980
but it reduces guesswork and makes local inference workflows more portable across compatible tools.
